{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "The internal-controls library in CatalogFile shape, so applyCatalogFile creates the Internal Control framework, its 23 category requirements, the pack, and the ICN template->requirement links together.",
    "why": "The 151 ICN-* templates were seeded as global ControlTemplates belonging to no framework and no pack. Their only route into a tenant was a side effect of installing SOME OTHER framework pack, which made installing ISO 27001 create 233 controls instead of 93 (see usecases/framework/install.ts). That sweep was removed, leaving the library seeded and unreachable. This file gives it a framework and a pack of its own, so a tenant installs it deliberately.",
    "grounding": "Codes, titles and categories are taken verbatim from internal-controls.json, which stays the source of truth for control CONTENT (objective, success criteria, testing methodology, related policies) — applyCatalogFile skips field updates on templates that already exist, and prisma/control-template-seed.ts writes those fields. Requirements are the 23 distinct categories the library already carries; nothing is invented here.",
    "tasksAreEmpty": "Deliberate. Authored tasks live on these templates already and are written by prisma/control-template-seed.ts. reconcileTemplateTasks returns early on an empty array, so this file cannot deprecate them.",
    "crossFrameworkMappings": "NOT duplicated here. Each control keeps its policy-mediated ISO 27001 / NIS2 requirement links from internal-controls-policy-framework-map.json; applyCatalogFile upserts links and never deletes, so a control ends up mapped to Internal Control AND to whichever standards its policies reach.",
    "deliveredBy": "scripts/seed-framework-catalogs.ts",
    "generated": "2026-09-09",
    "count": 151
  },
